Learning data (src/main/resources/static/learning/)
---------------------------------------------------

Contains data from OpenJLPT (CC BY-SA 4.0), which uses JMdict and KANJIDIC2
(EDRDG), Jonathan Waller's JLPT lists, and Tatoeba.

- OpenJLPT, https://github.com/evanclan/OpenJLPT
  Pinned revision 0d1d3410bec90bd4098a7c72de820543cb4f707c (v0.3.0).
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
  Full licence text: src/main/resources/static/learning/OpenJLPT-LICENSE.txt
  Upstream notice:   src/main/resources/static/learning/OpenJLPT-NOTICE.txt

- JMdict and KANJIDIC2, Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group
  (EDRDG), https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0.

- Jonathan Waller's JLPT lists, https://www.tanos.co.uk/jlpt/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution (as stated by the pinned OpenJLPT notice).

- Tatoeba, https://tatoeba.org (Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 FR).
  No Tatoeba example sentences are shipped in this release.

The files under src/main/resources/static/learning/ are a derived dataset and
are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0. They are separate from the MIT-licensed code.
Changes from the upstream source: search fields and stable kanji ids were
added; vocabulary example sentences and meaning multiple-choice questions were
withheld pending independent review; only reading questions verified to have a
single correct answer were kept.


Grammar checklist
-----------------

The N5–N3 coverage checklist is the grammar pages of the Wikibooks "JLPT Guide"
(compiled by Jonathan Waller), CC BY-SA 4.0. Only pattern names and levels
were used as a checklist; no explanations or examples were copied, and the
list itself is not included.


